# Per-route SPA HTML files (scripts/generate_route_html.mjs writes
# dist/<lang>/<route>/index.html for every SPA path × language) handle current
# routes automatically — Cloudflare serves the directory index. Below: legacy
# unprefixed URLs are 301-redirected to the English variant so existing Google
# index entries don't 404.
#
# Cloudflare Pages serves static assets first, so these rules only fire when
# no matching file exists in dist/. dist/index.html is a JS+meta redirect to
# /en/ so we deliberately do NOT add a "/ /en/ 301" rule — the dist file wins
# and gives crawlers a canonical signal too.
# Recover from stacked /ko/ko/ or /en/en/ URLs (caused by previous redirect-shell
# bug). Send the user to that language's root instead of looping.
/ko/ko/*                   /ko/                       301
/en/en/*                   /en/                       301
/ko/en/*                   /en/                       301
/en/ko/*                   /ko/                       301

/blog/*                    /en/blog/:splat            301
/gear/*                    /en/gear/:splat            301
/how-it-works              /en/how-it-works/          301
/about                     /en/about/                 301
/privacy                   /en/privacy/               301
/terms                     /en/terms/                 301
/affiliate-disclosure      /en/affiliate-disclosure/  301
/how-it-works/             /en/how-it-works/          301
/about/                    /en/about/                 301
/privacy/                  /en/privacy/               301
/terms/                    /en/terms/                 301
/affiliate-disclosure/     /en/affiliate-disclosure/  301
/blog                      /en/blog/                  301
